text:
{
  "summary": "Amy Cazin, who built natural deodorant company Primal Pit Paste from an initial $100, turned down Wal-Mart’s offer to carry her products because the young business wasn’t ready to supply a retailer on that scale. The company later grew to sell more than 75 products and became available at Whole Foods and thousands of independent retailers."
}

{
  "summary": "McLaren plans to spend £1 billion (about $1.45 billion) over six years on research and development, aiming to launch 15 new cars by 2022, including a P1 successor and an all-electric model. The investment will fund new powertrains and carbon-fiber structures as the company seeks to grow annual sales from 2,000 to 5,000."
}

{
  "summary": "The post is teasing why ceiling fans in India typically have three blades while those in the US often have four. Indian fans are generally lighter and spin faster to provide standalone cooling efficiently, whereas US fans tend to run more slowly to circulate air and supplement air conditioning."
}

{
  "summary": "Jessica Simpson wore a low-cut top, blazer, skinny jeans, and stilettos to dinner in Calabasas with fiancé Eric Johnson and daughter Maxwell; their infant son Ace stayed home. Three months after giving birth, she said she feels at peace as a mom and hinted she may return to music, tweeting, “I need to make music.”"
}

{
  "summary": "Leann tells her grandfather, Ried, that she’s expecting, and he bursts into tears when he sees the ultrasound. The surprise is that it shows twins—two baby girls, born in February 2016."
}

{
  "summary": "Saudi Arabia bought the most U.S. weapons from 2011 to 2015, followed closely by the United Arab Emirates. The rest of the top 10 were Turkey, South Korea, Australia, Taiwan, India, Singapore, Iraq, and Egypt."
}

{
  "summary": "Bill Maher urged TV hosts interviewing President-elect Donald Trump to treat him as a politician and hold him accountable rather than let him use their shows for publicity. Maher said he’d still welcome Trump on his own program, noting the unpredictable president-elect might appear soon."
}

{
  "summary": "BBC golf commentator Peter Alliss was caught on a hot mic saying Masters champion Sergio Garcia’s fiancée, Angela Akins, wore “the shortest skirt in the country,” then joking that the couple would have “some fun in the hotel tonight.” The BBC called the skirt remark inappropriate; the article also reviews Alliss’s history of controversial comments about women."
}

{
  "summary": "The post is teasing Eranna, a roughly 60-year-old man living in the forests of Tamil Nadu who is described as the last rat catcher in the area. He learned the traditional craft from his father and grandfather, catches field rats to protect farmers’ crops, and says he won’t teach the skill to the next generation."
}

{
  "summary": "A couple in Gujarat chose family planning after having 17 children—16 daughters and one son. The father kept hoping for another boy, but village elders persuaded him and his wife to stop expanding their family; she underwent a tubectomy."
}

{
  "summary": "A person filming Mike Tyson’s 1995 fight with a device that looks like a modern cameraphone is not a time traveler. It was likely one of several handheld cameras available at the time, such as the Casio QV-10A or Logitech Fotoman."
}

{
  "summary": "After hearing that abandoned babies in a Ugandan orphanage had stopped crying because no one came when they cried, Dayna promised to comfort her daughter whenever she needed her. That’s why her husband found her asleep in the baby’s crib: she had climbed in to soothe Luella."
}

{
  "summary": "An Argentine farmer unearthed the 10,000-year-old shell of a glyptodon, a giant armored mammal related to the armadillo that could weigh up to two tons. The fossil was found on his property in Carlos Spegazzini, near Buenos Aires."
}

{
  "summary": "A viral fan theory reimagines *Friends* as Phoebe Buffay’s drug-fueled fantasy: she is homeless and alone at Central Perk, watching Ross, Rachel, Monica, Joey, and Chandler and imagining herself as their friend throughout all 10 seasons. The post argues the show should have ended with Phoebe staring out the window, rather than the group leaving their apartment."
}

{
  "summary": "Speedrunner BubblesDelFuego set Fallout 4’s world record by completing the main story in a little over an hour. The run uses exploits such as climbing through walls with items, clipping through Power Armor, and a cover-slide glitch that teleports him across the map."
}

{
  "summary": "Legendary Simpsons writer John Swartzwelder’s Twitter account mostly promotes his detective novels by posting witty quotes from them, rather than writing new jokes for Twitter. The article wonders whether this blunt self-promotion is actually a dry, deadpan performance in itself."
}

{
  "summary": "The post is teasing that Shailene Woodley’s favorite word may be “badass.” She uses it repeatedly when talking about Divergent, her co-stars and stunt double, author Veronica Roth, and even the possibility of shaving her head."
}

{
  "summary": "The post is teasing why Apple buying Tesla would be a bad idea: Apple CEO Tim Cook and Tesla CEO Elon Musk have fundamentally incompatible leadership styles, and Musk would be unlikely to accept working for Apple or give up control of Tesla. A takeover would probably require Musk to leave, clashing with his goal of keeping Tesla independent."
}

{
  "summary": "The article says then Defence Minister Manohar Parrikar proposed creating all-women combat battalions across the Army, Navy and Air Force, arguing that dedicated women’s units could address resistance to women leading men. It also notes his support for gradually expanding women’s military opportunities, including entry through the National Defence Academy and Sainik schools."
}

{
  "summary": "The three longest routes then in operation were Air India’s San Francisco–Delhi flight (about 9,400 miles), Emirates’ Dubai–Auckland flight (8,820 miles), and Qantas’ Sydney–Dallas flight (8,577 miles). Qantas’s planned Perth–London service was expected to rank third when it launched, while a proposed Singapore–New York route could later take the distance record."
}

{
  "summary": "NPR visuals chief Brian Boyer’s team is developing Carebot, a tool to reward stories for meaningful impact rather than raw clicks. It would track signals such as how many readers finish a story, share it, or say they loved it—aiming to discourage misleading clickbait headlines and encourage journalism that makes people care."
}

{
  "summary": "Republican health care expert Avik Roy argues that the GOP is doomed because its post-1964 coalition and present-day base are rooted in white nationalism, a reality conservative intellectuals denied—helping pave the way for Trump. He predicts the party will either fracture or be replaced, and says conservatives must build a genuinely inclusive movement centered on individual liberty."
}

{
  "summary": "Rob Kardashian and Blac Chyna are reportedly expecting a girl, according to an anonymous source cited by Us Weekly. The couple had not publicly confirmed the news; their baby was due in October."
}

{
  "summary": "When scientists explored Romania’s Movile Cave, sealed off for about 5.5 million years, they found a toxic, sunless ecosystem containing 48 identified animal species, 33 found nowhere else. Many are eyeless and unpigmented, and the ecosystem is powered by chemosynthetic bacteria rather than sunlight."
}

{
  "summary": "At the 2017 Oscars, Faye Dunaway mistakenly announced *La La Land* as best picture before the award was corrected to *Moonlight*. Other highlights included Viola Davis’s emotional supporting-actress speech, Jimmy Kimmel’s Trump jokes, and Mahershala Ali’s win."
}

{
  "summary": "Lenovo’s Yoga Book replaces physical keys with a second touch surface that displays a glowing keyboard and trackpad with haptic feedback. That surface also works with a stylus to take notes, or digitizes handwriting instantly as you write on paper placed over it."
}

{
  "summary": "While tracking white-lipped peccaries in Brazil, researchers unexpectedly found caves containing ancient rock art, likely 4,000 to 10,000 years old. The drawings show people, geometric shapes, armadillos, birds, reptiles and other animals—but no peccaries."
}

{
  "summary": "The post teases advice for getting rid of earworms—songs that loop in your head. The article recommends avoiding repetitive or recently heard music, chewing gum, changing your walking pace, singing a different song, choosing music to suit your mood, socializing, and, if needed, stopping the struggle and distracting yourself."
}

{
  "summary": "Candice Swanepoel will wear the 2013 Victoria’s Secret Fantasy Bra, a $10 million ruby, diamond and yellow-sapphire set made with more than 4,200 gems in 18-karat gold. Its matching belt features a 52-carat ruby, and the red-and-blue “Royal Fantasy Bra” will close the fashion show."
}

{
  "summary": "The weird white, stringy cords attached to a raw egg’s yolk are called chalazae. They anchor the yolk in place, are edible, and are usually more visible in fresh eggs; they fade as an egg ages."
}

{
  "summary": "After nine years of grinding, Tibia player Kharsek reached level 999 and passed through the game’s legendary expertise door. He then logged off without revealing what was inside, leaving the secret unknown; developers say it isn’t a whole end-game feature or content package."
}

{
  "summary": "Netflix will exclusively stream “The Square,” an acclaimed documentary about the Egyptian protest in Cairo’s Tahrir Square, starting early next year. The Oscar contender’s early, exclusive streaming window marks a bigger step into film distribution for Netflix."
}

{
  "summary": "The post teases seven home purchases worth paying extra for: window coverings, linens and towels, upholstered furniture, a room-size rug, a mattress, original artwork, and countertops. The article explains why quality matters for each and suggests budget-friendly alternatives, such as tailored ready-made curtains, secondhand furniture, and a countertop in charcoal-gray Corian instead of granite."
}

{
  "summary": "Elite Dangerous: Horizons launches on Xbox One June 3 for $30 as an upgrade, or as a $30 Commander Deluxe edition that includes the base game. It bundles Planetary Landings and The Engineers; the latter reaches PC May 26 alongside a major free update, and Frontier outlined future features including multicrew, customizable commanders, and ship-launched fighters."
}

{
  "summary": "YouTubers GismoSlip froze a Galaxy Note 7 in ice for over 23 hours, then dropped it from 100 feet. The phone survived without a scratch and remained fully functional."
}

{
  "summary": "Julie Andrews is happy that Emily Blunt will play Mary Poppins in *Mary Poppins Returns*, telling director Rob Marshall, “Oh, wonderful!” Blunt said Andrews’ approval was lovely and eased the pressure of taking over the iconic role."
}
